Two things I would like to see in nethack (one of which I
reckon would be a good game feature, the other of which
is IMHO cute):

1) I was wandering around with a Priest and came across a
throne room--now the message that I would most like to see
in that situation would be if the king, as well as pounding
his sceptre, would say "Is there no-one who will rid me of
this trouble-some priest?" Can't be that hard to put in,
and it would really kill me :-)

2) A more useful feature--As it stands, if you kick/break/
throw/destroy/whatever a potion the vapour escapes and can
affect you. Now what I would like to see is if you get the
message "You hear a muffled shatter" when you kick open
chests/boxes, when you _open_ it the vapour escapes and
can then also affect you. It would make potential theives
think twice about opening it (or at least opening it
immediatly) as apart from the loss of a few potions is
no real deterrant to rampant vanalism... Theives
and Tourists and those would be advantaged and the
rest of the populace would have to think about the IMHO
now too easy way of getting into a chest someone has
carefully locked.

Comments?

Edouard.


